  - [1mB. Shortcuts inline, the rest in a "Filters" popover.[0m The two common cases stay one click away. Active filters show
    as removable tags. It's more compact, but the date range is one click further away.
  - [1mC. Sidebar.[0m The filters stay in view while you scroll, but they take width from a six-column table. On narrow
    screens the sidebar would have to collapse above the table anyway.

  I recommend A. Looking at one week is one of the three main jobs, so hiding the dates in a popover works against it. A
  is also the simplest to build and to make keyboard-accessible.

  The wireframes use rough placeholder styling. The real page will use only guideline tokens.

  You can click an option in the browser, and either way please reply here.

